==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|tenable|lang=fr}}, from {{term|tenir||to hold|lang=fr}}; compare {{term|tenible|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɛn.ə.bəl/}} {{SAMPA|/"tEn.@.b@l/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|of a theory, argument etc}}  capable of being [[maintained]] or [[justified]]; [[well-founded]]
#: ''Back in the 1800s, many did not consider Darwin's theory of evolution to be '''tenable''' at all.''
# {{context|of a defensive structure}} capable of being [[defended]] against [[assault]] or [[attack]]; [[defensible]]

====Antonyms====
* [[untenable]]

